# FILE(1)

## NAME

file - determine file type

## SYNOPSIS

| **file** [ **-f** listfile ] file ...

## DESCRIPTION

*File* performs a series of tests on each argument in an attempt to classify it. If an argument
appears to be text, *file* examines the first 512 bytes and tries to guess its language.

With **-f**, the names to be classified are read one per line from *listfile* instead of being
given as arguments.

## THE MAGIC NUMBERS ARE THIS MACHINE'S

*Note:* this is the one place *file* is not a faithful port of v7's. A header field here is one
48-bit word, six bytes, most significant first, and the magic is the one field whose high half
is not zero padding: **FMAGIC** is **BESM** 01 07 and **NMAGIC** is **BESM** 01 08
(*doc/File_Magic.md*, *cross/besm6/b.out.h*). *File* answers:

**pure executable**
: **NMAGIC**: read-only const and text, page-aligned data. Only **/bin/sh** and
  **/usr/test/puret** are built this way.

**executable**
: **FMAGIC** with **RELFLG** set - a fully linked program.

**relocatable object**
: **FMAGIC** without it. v7's *file* could not draw this distinction at all; it read a symbol
  table and nothing else.

**archive**
: **ARMAG**. The value is v7's; the width is not, so an archive begins 00 00 00 00 FF 65.

**not stripped** is appended when the symbol table is not empty. The PDP-11 magic numbers 0407,
0410, 0411, 0177555 and 0177545 are gone; the first three name nothing here and the last two
are the archive above and its predecessor.

## UTF-8 IS TEXT

*Note:* the second deliberate change, and the one a user meets. v7 declares any file containing
a byte with the eighth bit set to be **data**, and appends **with garbage** to anything else
that has one. This machine's text is UTF-8 end to end, so that reports the system's own Russian
prose as binary. Here the high-bit runs are validated as UTF-8 instead: a well-formed file is
text and a malformed byte is still **data**. A file that is valid UTF-8 but is not all ASCII is
reported as **text** rather than **ascii text**, which is the honest word for it.

## THE LANGUAGE TABLES ARE THIS MACHINE'S TOO

The assembler keywords are *b6as*'s directives (**.globl**, **.const**, **.text**, **.data**,
**.bss**, **.comm**, **.half**, **.word**, **.equ**, **.ascii**, **.strng**, **.org**) and its
Madlen mnemonics (**atx**, **xta**, **uj**, **vtm**, **vjm**), where v7's were PDP-11
pseudo-ops and PDP-11 instructions. **.even** is gone, a word machine having nothing to align
to, and so is **troff output**: there is no *troff* in this source tree - see *cmd/TODO.md*.

## SEE ALSO

ar(1), ld(1), strip(1)

## BUGS

It often makes mistakes. In particular it often suggests that command files are C programs.

Only the first 512 bytes are examined, so a file whose first block is ordinary text is ordinary
text whatever follows it.
